  Note over A,DB: 2026-12-01T00:00:01Z, card-fee v2 in effect, v1 still PUBLISHED
  par same moment, ordinary transactions, no advisory lock
    A->>DB: UPDATE ... WHERE old.status = 'PUBLISHED' ... RETURNING
    DB-->>A: v1, superseded_by 2 (row locked)
  and
    B->>DB: UPDATE ... WHERE old.status = 'PUBLISHED' ... RETURNING
    Note over B,DB: waits on the row lock of v1
  end
  A->>DB: INSERT history RETIRED (system, SUPERSEDED, 2), then outbox rules.version.retired.v1
  A->>DB: COMMIT
  DB-->>B: re-checks v1 on the committed row, status RETIRED, returns no row
  B->>DB: COMMIT, nothing written
  Note over A,DB: Retire by hand: bob retires v2 on replica A
  A->>DB: SELECT v2 FOR UPDATE, status PUBLISHED, lockVersion matches
  alt a newer version in effect supersedes v2
    A-->>A: 409 INVALID_STATE before any write
  else v2 in force or scheduled
    A->>DB: supersession for card-fee first, while v2 is still PUBLISHED
    A->>DB: UPDATE v2 RETIRED, retired_at now, history RETIRED (bob, reason, single), outbox event
    A->>DB: COMMIT, every replica stops selecting v2
